 ('0c810646-0f7d-5e9e-84dd-5116ec9750b2', '2025-2026', 36270, 39870, 1163, 16598, 1460, true, 129, 8675, true, false, 'CDS G1 (2025-26): out-of-state $36,270, nonresident $39,870, fees $1,163, food and housing $16,598 (the in-state tuition line is blank in the CDS). H6: need-based and non-need-based institutional aid are both available to nonresidents; 129 degree-seeking nonresident undergraduates received aid (avg $8,675).; Undergraduates receive an automatic merit scholarship of $5,000-$10,000 per year (GPA-based; headline on the first-year page). International Admissions also lists additional merit awards by application (up to $8,000/yr), donor awards and need-based grants; that table is labelled aid year 2022-23, so award names and status may be out of date. Estimated international cost of attendance for 2026-27 is about $60,852-$63,062 per year depending on school/college (tuition and fees $33,439-$35,649; 9 months, 12 credits).', '81a27f12-9c02-549d-8a77-7be2e12c7439');
