 ('907386ed-a5b4-53d3-92e0-6ec7d55d8e88', '2025-2026', 22187, 20541, 5040, 697, 657, 7479, 7037, 14011, 12847, 7.1, 50.7, 3.71, 98, '{"4.0": 38, "3.75-3.99": 21, "3.50-3.74": 17, "3.25-3.49": 12, "3.00-3.24": 7, "2.50-2.99": 4, "2.0-2.49": 1, "1.0-1.99": 0}'::jsonb, 'CDS C1 residency split (in-state 7,479 / out-of-state 14,011 / international 697 applicants; international admit rate computed 657/697 = 94.3%, 157 enrolled). Undergrad enrollment and intl count are the B2 ''Total Undergraduates'' column (22,544; nonresident 690). No early decision or early action; no waitlist. Admission is formula-style: students are assured admission with a 3.25+ GPA, or ACT 21 / SAT 1060 with a 2.0+ GPA (CDS C6); international applicants are admitted at a 2.5 GPA per the international admissions page.', 'd2d94904-8d37-534f-9daf-fc3550013cc8');
