 ('1532a872-1f5b-5818-af57-e857d8bb7a85', '2023-2024', 20918, 17353, 2463, 2081, 1839, 12558, 10044, 6279, 5470, 28, 2, 3.5, 99.9, '{"4.0": 20, "3.75-3.99": 13, "3.50-3.74": 13, "3.25-3.49": 16, "3.00-3.24": 15, "2.50-2.99": 20, "2.0-2.49": 2}'::jsonb, 'CDS C1 (fall 2023 entering class). This is the newest CDS UMass Boston had posted on its Common Data Set page when checked (2023-2024; no 2024-25 or 2025-26 file listed), so the figures are two cycles old. Residency split: in-state 12,558 / out-of-state 6,279 / international 2,081 applicants; 10,044 / 5,470 / 1,839 admitted; 1,968 / 287 / 208 enrolled. Undergrad enrollment and nonresident count are the B1/B2 ''Total Undergraduates'' figures (12,234; 844 international). CDS C6 marks admission as open for most students with selective admission to some programs. SAT/ACT percentiles cover only the 28% (695) / 2% (54) of enrollees who submitted scores; the GPA ''all enrolled'' column sums to 99%. CDS C14 (2023-24): priority date 11/1, closing date 2/15.', 'aad08275-83bc-5367-8be4-b247408d8a22');
