 ('6d87d36e-d608-5dc1-8126-add453253093', '2025-2026', 8673, 20823, 2990, 11194, 1120, 'merit_only', false, 1075, 5928, false, true, 'CDS G1 first-year full-year amounts (nonresident tuition equals out-of-state $20,823; per credit hour $685 nonresident vs $280 in-state). The CDS marks 2026-27 costs as not yet available, so these are most likely 2025-26 amounts. CDS H6: only institutional non-need-based aid is available to nonresidents; 1,075 degree-seeking nonresident undergraduates received it (avg $5,928). CDS C7 rows for test scores, essay and recommendations were left unmarked, so they are omitted.; UNT Excellence Scholarship ($2,000-$12,000 a year by class rank and unweighted GPA, renewable up to 4 years, +$1,000 bonus for SAT 1350/ACT 30) and the $1,000-a-year UNT Achievement Scholarship are automatic for first-time freshmen admitted by the priority date; the page states they apply to international students too. International recipients may get a Texas competitive scholarship waiver covering the difference between in-state and out-of-state tuition (Selective Service requirement applies where relevant). The CDS reports institutional aid for nonresidents as non-need-based only.', '4083c2ec-ac9d-53fe-9cc7-9ea706caa697');
