 ('839eb235-b785-5929-9260-730c382b6cd3', '2026-2027', 7704, 23022, 23022, 2068, 11500, 1200, 'need_aware_limited', true, 373, 10216, false, 'CDS G1 first-year full-year amounts for 2026-27 (nonresident tuition equals out-of-state; per credit hour $787 nonresident vs $262 in-state). The $11,500 food-and-housing line is printed without a label in the extracted text and is read as on-campus food and housing. CDS H6: institutional need-based and non-need-based aid exists for nonresidents; 373 degree-seeking nonresident undergraduates received aid (avg $10,216, total $3,810,516).; UTEP''s catalog calls financial assistance for international students limited. Citizens of Mexico who meet the PASE requirements might qualify to pay Texas resident tuition. CDS H6 reports institutional need-based and non-need-based aid for nonresidents (373 recipients, avg $10,216). No international merit scholarship amounts were found on UTEP''s admissions pages.', '9bf484cd-6913-5249-9a82-5c4913afb007');
