 ('c5aed17b-a2ae-55b9-92f7-a6d1c4954772', '2024-2025', 9011, 22051, 14912, 1000, 3002, 'need_aware_limited', true, 340, 6646, false, true, 'IPEDS College Navigator 2024-25 first-time undergraduate expenses: tuition amounts include required fees; on-campus food and housing $14,912. The CDS left section G (costs) blank. CDS 2024-25 H6: 340 degree-seeking nonresident undergraduates received institutional aid (avg $6,646, total $2,259,506); the CDS did not mark whether it was need- or non-need-based.; International students are not eligible for federal aid. The merit-based Distinguished Presidential Scholarship for fall freshmen admitted by Jan. 15 pays $500-$6,000 a year by class rank and SAT/ACT (e.g. top 20% with 1170 SAT / 24 ACT: $2,500; top 25% with 1150 / 24: $500; applicants without scores go to committee review) and is valued up to $24,000 over four years; nonresident/international recipients of at least $1,000 a year get a nonresident tuition waiver while eligibility is maintained. The need-based International Student Grant requires F-1/J-1 status and full-time enrollment; the Good Neighbor Program covers tuition for eligible Western Hemisphere countries (its current funding status is unconfirmed).', 'f953140b-bb91-57e5-9944-e409e7449b45');
